    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0524" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1121 Fernandez, Antonio/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-08T10:00:00+00:00">June 8, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 8—7:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s June 5, 2 p.m. Antonio Fernandez Villa. General Queipo de
                        Llano<anchor n="71" xml:id="d469-f1"/> promised me last night he would
                    instruct military authorities in Palma de Mallorca to postpone trial of
                    Fernandez pending investigation by an American consular officer to be sent
                    there.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d469-f1" n="71" xml:id="d469-f1-content">
                <p>Nationalist general, in command at Seville.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
